# =====================================================================
# hermes-runtime-bridge / Agent Execution Engine (AEE) — .gitignore
# Generated for AEE-0 baseline hardening (2026-07-10)
#
# Layered rules:
#   1) secrets / credentials (NEVER commit)
#   2) runtime data (DB, logs, reports, .venv)
#   3) build / tooling artifacts
#   4) local-only convenience
# =====================================================================

# ---------- 1. Secrets / credentials ----------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.api_keys.vault.json
**/.api_keys.vault.json
CREDENTIALS.txt
**/CREDENTIALS.txt
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
secrets/
private/

# ---------- 2. Runtime data ----------
# ---------- 2. Runtime data ----------
# SQLite DBs (WAL + SHM sidecar) under data/
data/*.db
data/*.db-journal
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
# Pre-rebuild DB backups under data/ (e.g. dispatcher.db.pre-rebuild-20260711T152000Z{,-shm,-wal})
data/*.pre-rebuild*
# Root-level runtime DB (legacy path; data/ is the canonical location)
/dispatcher.db
/dispatcher.db-journal
/dispatcher.db-wal
/dispatcher.db-shm
# Runtime evidence capture directory
/AEE_GPT_E2E_EVIDENCE/
# Hash receipts generated alongside root-level work-order reports
/*.sha256
# Local-only runtime_data (introduced in AEE-0)
runtime_data/
# Logs
logs/
*.log
# Per-task reports
reports/TASK-*/
# Generated report sidecar/envelope JSON (e.g. *_verification_sidecar.json,
# *_cli_smoke_envelope.json). Tracked report specs are all .md, so .json in
# reports/ is always generated — ignore to reduce git status noise.
# Evidence: 2 untracked reports/*.json at audit; 0 tracked reports/*.json.
/reports/*.json
# Backups
*.bak.*
*.bak-*
data.bak.*/

# ---------- 2b. Dependency lockfile policy (TD-001) ----------
# Lockfiles and dependency specs are INTENTIONALLY TRACKED, not ignored.
# Per README §"Dependency management" (lines 188-202):
#   requirements.in         → requirements.lock         (Linux)
#   requirements-dev.in     → requirements-dev.lock     (dev)
#   requirements.lock.darwin                            (macOS)
#   constraints.txt          — version upper bounds
#   scripts/compile-deps.sh — regenerate lockfiles (uv pip compile)
#   scripts/verify-deps.sh   — read-only lockfile verification
# These files SHOULD be committed in a separate work order (WO-1-AC).
# Do NOT add ignore rules for requirements.* / constraints.txt / scripts/.

# ---------- 3. Build / tooling artifacts ----------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
node_modules/

# ---------- 4. Local-only convenience ----------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.tmp_*.py
